v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2
* sky130-bandgap error amplifier -- symbol (issue #8, contents redesigned by #9).
*
* A single-stage current-mirror OTA on 5 V thick-oxide devices, sized to the
* offset/mismatch budget in design/error-amp-offset-budget.md. This symbol is
* the swap boundary that #8 created and #9 used: error_amp.sch was replaced
* wholesale, THIS FILE WAS NOT -- the pin list below is unchanged, so
* design/bandgap_core.sch did not have to be re-entered. Keep it that way:
* any future amplifier (chopped, auto-zeroed, trimmed) should arrive the same
* way, behind this interface.
*
* Pin order below is the order xschem emits into @pinlist, which is also the
* .subckt port order. Do not reorder without updating error_amp.sch.
*   VINP  non-inverting input  (AOUT rises when VINP rises)
*   VINN  inverting input
*   AOUT  output (high impedance; drives a PMOS gate in the core)
*   ITAIL tail-current input (the core mirrors the amp's bias from its own
*         output branch, so the amp needs no separate bias network)
*   VDD   supply
*   VSS   ground
}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
L 4 -40 -50 -40 50 {}
L 4 -40 -50 40 0 {}
L 4 -40 50 40 0 {}
L 4 -50 -20 -40 -20 {}
L 4 -50 20 -40 20 {}
L 4 40 0 50 0 {}
L 4 -10 -50 -10 -35 {}
L 4 10 -50 10 -30 {}
L 4 0 50 0 25 {}
B 5 -52.5 -22.5 -47.5 -17.5 {name=VINP dir=in}
B 5 -52.5 17.5 -47.5 22.5 {name=VINN dir=in}
B 5 47.5 -2.5 52.5 2.5 {name=AOUT dir=out}
B 5 -12.5 -52.5 -7.5 -47.5 {name=ITAIL dir=inout}
B 5 7.5 -52.5 12.5 -47.5 {name=VDD dir=inout}
B 5 -2.5 47.5 2.5 52.5 {name=VSS dir=inout}
T {@name} -35 -70 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {@symname} -35 60 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {+} -34 -26 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {-} -34 14 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {ITAIL} -30 -46 0 0 0.2 0.2 {layer=7}
T {VDD} 14 -46 0 0 0.2 0.2 {layer=7}
T {VSS} 4 38 0 0 0.2 0.2 {layer=7}
T {AOUT} 22 -10 0 0 0.2 0.2 {layer=7}
